Description: The monitors' 3D options are the layer's Enable 3D and Display Settings
 "A program's 3D options are only: enable 3D, render resolution per eye, and a
 shortcut to Display Settings." The monitors' Preview choice (Packed Frame as It Is,
 Left Eye Only, 3D) becomes the stereo layer's own "Enable 3D"
 (Stereo::Enable3DAction, the switch and the words every program on the layer has),
 the view of the left eye below it (choosing it enables 3D again, as in the picture
 programs of ORDER 551c), and "Display Settings…", which opens Display Configuration
 (kcmshell6 kcm_kscreen), where each screen's 3D format and its swap of the eyes are.
 The setting keeps its values: 0 is Enable 3D off (the frames as they are, nothing
 declared), 1 the left eye, 2 3D; a choice saved before reads the same.
 The project's own "Right Eye First" goes: the definitive swap is the output's and a
 program has no swap for everything; the eye order is each clip's (its input format
 and swap). A project saved with it gets the declared packing with the right eye
 first as the input format of each of its video clips, takes its packing from its
 clips, and the person is told once in the project monitor. A packing declared for
 the project is left eye first.
